.TH IDLE-GARDEN 1 "2026" "idle-garden 0.4.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
idle-garden \- an ASCII tree slowly grows over your screen while you are away
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B idle-garden
[\fIOPTIONS\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B idle-garden
runs in the background of your desktop session. When the mouse and keyboard
have not been touched for a while, a fullscreen window appears on every monitor
and an ASCII tree starts growing from a small patch of earth: a trunk, a crown,
branches, vines and ivy, until the whole screen is overgrown. Any mouse
movement, click or key press makes it disappear instantly. It never locks the
session.
.PP
It starts automatically after login. Run without options to start it by hand.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-preview
Show the tree right now, fullscreen. Move the mouse to close it.
.TP
.B \-\-terminal
Grow a tree inside the current terminal. Press any key to quit.
.TP
.BI \-g " MINUTES" "\fR, \fP" \-\-grow\-minutes " MINUTES"
Minutes until the tree fills the screen (default 40).
.TP
.BI \-t " SECONDS" "\fR, \fP" \-\-timeout " SECONDS"
Seconds without input before the tree appears (default 120).
.TP
.BI \-\-theme " auto|dark|light"
Colour theme. \fBauto\fR (default) follows the system light/dark style.
.TP
.BI \-\-season " auto|spring|summer|autumn|winter"
Season of the garden. \fBauto\fR (default) follows today's date.
.TP
.B \-\-no\-animals
No birds or butterflies.
.TP
.BI \-\-font\-size " PIXELS"
Size of the ASCII characters (default 18).
.TP
.B \-\-restart
Restart the background app, for example after editing the settings.
.TP
.B \-\-stop
Stop the background app until the next login.
.TP
.B \-\-check
Show how idle time is detected on this desktop.
.TP
.B \-\-edit\-config
Create the settings file if needed and print its path.
.TP
.B \-V, \-\-version
Print the version.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.config/idle-garden/config.ini
Settings: timeout, grow_minutes, font, font_size, theme,
dark_background, light_background, season, hemisphere, animals, wind,
respect_inhibit, keep_screen_on.
.SH EXAMPLES
.TP
.B idle-garden \-\-preview \-g 2
Watch a whole tree grow in two minutes.
.TP
.B idle-garden \-\-terminal
Grow a tree in the terminal.
.SH SEE ALSO
https://github.com/DMgen10/idle-garden
